.TH "REPROCTL\-AUTONOMY" "1" "2026" "reproctl" "Repro Development Tools"
.SH NAME
reproctl\-autonomy \- durable local claim, status, and control state
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]reproctl autonomy\f[R] \f[I]subcommand\f[R] [\f[I]options\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage durable local state for autonomous orchestration.
.PP
The autonomy surface records local claims, active runs, retry metadata,
and Linear sync state for operator workflows.
It does not provide a web UI.
.SS Actor model
The claim queue is shared by three actors:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]User/operator\f[R] \(em inspects state, discovers work, and
overrides lifecycle state when needed.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Bot\-mode intake\f[R] \(em discovers and claims work up to policy
and concurrency limits.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Delivery daemon\f[R] \(em operates only on already\-claimed work
and shepherds it through prepare, run, retry, reconcile, release, and
cancel.
.PP
Commands are owned by the actor that mutates the relevant part of the
contract.
Discovery and claim are intake primitives; prepare and run are daemon
lifecycle primitives; release, cancel, retry, and reconcile are daemon
recovery or terminal controls with operator override use.
